dict(day=12, filename="p1-day-12-stationary-points.pdf", kicker="AS MATHEMATICS - PURE 1 - DAY 12", title="Stationary points", subtitle="Turning points and optimisation", aim="Find, classify and interpret stationary points.", intro="At a stationary point, the tangent is horizontal, so dy/dx=0.", notes=["Solve dy/dx=0 to find stationary x-values.", "Substitute into y to find coordinates.", "Second derivative positive: local minimum; negative: local maximum.", "A sign change + to - is a maximum; - to + is a minimum."], memory="Differentiate, equal zero, solve, substitute, classify.", worked=[("Classify","y=x^2-4x+1. dy/dx=2x-4=0 gives x=2; y=-3. d2y/dx2=2>0, so minimum (2,-3)."),("Cubic","y=x^3-3x: dy/dx=3x^2-3=0 gives x=+-1.")], questions=["1. Find stationary point of y=x^2+6x+2.","2. Classify it.","3. Find stationary x-values of y=x^3-12x.","4. Find and classify both stationary points in Q3.","5. Find minimum value of x^2-8x+20.","6. Rectangle perimeter is 20. If sides are x and 10-x, find maximum area."], answers=["dy/dx=2x+6=0, x=-3; y=-7.","d2y/dx2=2>0, so a minimum.","3x^2-12=0, so x=+-2.","At x=-2, y=16 and second derivative -12: maximum. At x=2, y=-16 and second derivative 12: minimum.","Stationary x=4; minimum value 4.","A=x(10-x)=10x-x^2. A'=10-2x=0 gives x=5; maximum area 25."], footer="Rohan Study System | P1 Day 12"),
